# DSP patterns for logue SDK

## Approved patterns

### 1. Oscillator phase accumulation (fixed-point)

```c
static uint32_t s_phase;
const uint32_t w = osc_w0(params->pitch);

for (uint32_t i = 0; i < frames; i++) {
  yn[i] = (q31_t)(s_phase - 0x80000000U);
  s_phase += w;
}
```

### 2. Parameter smoothing (one-pole)

```c
static float s_smooth;
float target = /* from OSC_PARAM */;
s_smooth += (target - s_smooth) * 0.001f;   // coefficient tuned per parameter
```

### 3. Buffer-aligned effect processing

```c
void MODFX_PROCESS(const float *main_xn, float *main_yn,
                   const float *sub_xn, float *sub_yn,
                   uint32_t frames) {
  for (uint32_t i = 0; i < frames; i++) {
    // process exactly `frames` samples — never more, never less
  }
}
```

## Anti-patterns (never generate)

- malloc / new / std::vector in audio callbacks.
- printf / fprintf in production units.
- while (1) inside PROCESS or CYCLE.
- Division inside per-sample loops without precomputed reciprocals.
- Assuming frames is always 16 or 32; it varies (support up to 64 on v1.1.0).
- Using double on Cortex-M4 targets (no hardware double FPU).

## Real-time budget guidance

- Total CPU budget for a user unit: ≤ 40% of one core on Cortex-M4.
- Leave headroom: the SDK and host synth consume the rest.
- Profile with the SDK's built-in cycle counter if available.
